# Release signers — the SSH public keys allowed to sign a release's SHA256SUMS
# (deploy/lib/verify-release.sh; docs/deploy.md, "Release trust"; audit v6, PROC-5).
#
# One key per line, in ssh-keygen's allowed-signers format:
#
#   <who> namespaces="rand-release" <key type> <base64 public key>
#
# for example (not a real key):
#
#   release-officer@randprotocol namespaces="rand-release" sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com AAAA…
#
# Rules:
#   - PUBLIC keys only. The private half never touches this repository, the build host or CI.
#     It is held off the build host, preferably hardware-backed (ed25519-sk / ecdsa-sk).
#   - Adding or removing a line is a reviewed change to this file: whoever is listed here can
#     authorise a binary that runs as root on the fleet.
#   - THIS FILE LISTS NO KEY YET (2026-09-30). Until the operator adds one, verify_release_sums
#     refuses every release, and the roll scripts install only with ALLOW_UNSIGNED=1.
